From 698d097b221447ee6f3e95e09f8ca7729b4a2bf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:31:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] oneshot: trace all collectives, split CTA-0 wait, and export
 Perfetto

Extend SPARKNET_ROCE_TRACE across allgather, reducescatter, and exchange
with op-kind metadata in W_META, separate CTA-0 RDMA peer flag polling
(roce_wait_peers) from non-zero CTA local barrier waiting (roce_wait_cta0)
with warp-0 synchronization for IKET lane-0 accuracy, and add NTP-aligned
Chrome/Perfetto timeline export (perfetto_events, export_perfetto).

Upstream-Base: 1fd6a1fbd8dc4884057046d1ebd93d585c9e4bcf
Rationale: SPARKNET_ROCE_TRACE previously instrumented only oneshot_allreduce,
leaving allgather, reducescatter, and exchange untraced, while calling
roce_wait_peers from every CTA caused TileLang IKET to label non-zero CTA
local barrier spins as wait.flags.
Quality-Implications: None. Untraced kernels (SPARKNET_ROCE_TRACE=0, default)
compile without trace calls and cache separately; traced kernels preserve
identical collective semantics and bit-exact outputs.
Tests: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests; pytest tests/gpu/test_oneshot_gpu.py
Upstream-Status: Candidate for dgx-spark-networking main.
